message: "If you use Catalejo, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "Catalejo Genómico: a platform for exploring curated collections of microbial genomes"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/[ORGANIZATION]/catalejo"
authors:
  - family-names: "Ugalde"
    given-names: "Juan A."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6638-0817"
    affiliation: "Facultad de Ingenieria, Universidad del Desarrollo"
keywords:
  - microbial genomics
  - antimicrobial resistance
  - genome visualization
  - pangenome
  - bacterial genomes
abstract: >-
  Catalejo Genómico is a web platform for looking at a curated collection of
  microbial genomes produced by the mgap pipeline, with their annotation,
  resistance determinants, mobile elements, typing results, pangenomes,
  phylogenies and embeddings. Releases are immutable and reproducible, and the
  application reads them directly in the browser.
